// SETUP REQUIRED:
// 1. Create a Firebase project at https://console.firebase.google.com
// 2. Add an Android app with applicationId "com.streamflow.app"
// 3. Download the generated google-services.json
// 4. Replace this file — save it as "google-services.json" (drop the .SAMPLE
//    extension) directly in the app/ directory, next to build.gradle.kts.
//
// Until this file is in place, the project will not build because the
// com.google.gms.google-services Gradle plugin (applied in app/build.gradle.kts)
// requires a real google-services.json to run.
//
// Firebase is only needed starting Phase 1.5 (Auth, Firestore) per the
// Implementation Plan — the MVP screens run entirely on MockCatalogRepository
// and don't touch Firebase yet, so you can strip the Firebase plugin/deps
// from app/build.gradle.kts if you want a Firebase-free build for now.
